## Statistic inference for Figure 7 (Senovilla-Ganzo et al., 2026)

In most cases, single cell datasets lack enough biological replicates to consider them as statistical N. Although single cells could be consider as biological replicates, their large number and sequencing biases could lead to biased conclusions in classical statistical tests. Complementary to these classical tests, we propose permutations tests in-between the compared biological classes for Wilcox or non-parametric Mann-Whitney (pair-wise) and 1-way ANOVA or non-parametric Kruskal-Wallis (more than two groups, developmental comparisons).

